<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="0">
<!--
    N1 (RALPLAN 2026-07-23): deliberately EMPTY in this first pass.

    The original plan called for an "idempotent Document Layout config
    record" capturing brand tokens (colour/font/logo/paperformat) as
    versioned data. That record must NEVER set
    res.company.external_report_layout_id and must NEVER set any
    company-level font/colour field the stock web.external_layout
    dispatcher reads - doing so would restyle every not-yet-bridged report
    globally at Phase 1 (the exact N1-residual risk the consensus plan
    exists to avoid).

    Because the finalized design applies brand tokens per-bridge via CSS
    (see sgc_report_blocks.scss, consumed only inside .o_sgc_report) rather
    than via res.company fields, no such record is actually required for
    Phase 1 to function. This file is kept as an explicit, empty,
    trivially-idempotent placeholder so the manifest's data list and the
    plan's "idempotent config record, no drift" acceptance criterion both
    have a concrete, checkable artifact - loading it twice is a guaranteed
    no-op. If a future phase needs a real res.company-scoped record (e.g.
    for the Settings > Document Layout picker to show useful brand values),
    add it here explicitly and re-run the idempotent-load test.
-->
</odoo>
